    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d544">

                <pb facs="0747" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Korea)/5–1546</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chinese
                        Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Koo</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Acting Secretary of State presents his compliments to His Excellency the
                    Chinese Ambassador and has the honor to refer to his predecessor’s note of May
                    15, 1946, and to the Secretary of State’s note to the Chinese Ambassador of May
                    31, 1946<anchor n="47" xml:id="d544-f1"/> regarding the establishment of Chinese
                    representation at Seoul, Korea.</p>
                <p>The Acting Secretary of State is now able to inform the Chinese Ambassador that
                    the American Embassy at Nanking is being instructed to invite the Chinese
                    Foreign Office to designate a Chinese Consular Official and two assistants to
                    establish a small Consular Office at Seoul to perform limited consular and
                    liaison functions in the area of Korea presently under United States military
                        jurisdiction.<anchor n="48" xml:id="d544-f2"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-09-06">September 6,
                        1946</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d544-f1" n="47" xml:id="d544-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d544-f2" n="48" xml:id="d544-f2-content">
                <p>The note to the Chinese Government was telegraphed to Seoul in telegram 118.
                    September 5, 1946. Notes also were sent to the British and French Governments,
                    outlining limitations under which consular officers would function.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
